

# ── Subject ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# One line, conventional commit:  type(scope): summary
#   type   feat fix chore docs refactor perf test ci build revert
#   scope  optional, the area touched — auth, quote, admin, invoice, deps
#   summary imperative and lower case, no trailing period, under ~72 chars
#
# ── Body ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Four sentences or fewer, in prose. Cover:
#   why   the problem, or the reason this change exists
#   what  what the change does
#   how   the approach — only if the diff does not make it obvious
# Leave the body out entirely for a change whose subject already says it all
# (a typo, a version bump). Do not restate the diff file by file.
#
# ── Refs ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Last line, when there is anything to point at. Issues, PRs, docs:
#   Refs: #19, #28, docs/local-stack.md
#   Closes: #6
# Omit the line when there is nothing to reference.
